    <li><b>Update date first.</b> A course last updated before mid-2024 will teach outdated exam objectives. 220-1201 was updated in 2025; prefer 2025–2026 content.</li>

    <li><b>Check exam version alignment.</b> Ensure the course explicitly covers <b>220-1201</b> (not the older 220-1101). The 1201 adds cloud concepts, enhanced security, and modern mobile hardware coverage.</li>

    <li><b>Read the newest reviews.</b> Sort reviews by newest and look for comments from the last three months — they flag syllabus changes, broken lab links, or updated hardware coverage.</li>

    <li><b>Inspect the curriculum vs exam objectives.</b> Map each course section to the official CompTIA 220-1201 domains: Mobile Devices (13%), Networking (23%), Hardware (25%), Virtualization and Cloud (11%), Hardware and Network Troubleshooting (28%). Skipping any domain is a risk.</li>

    <li><b>Judge the instructor's track record.</b> Dion Training Solutions has 3M+ total enrollments across A+ courses. Look for instructors with high overall review counts, not just this course.</li>

