  <h2>What you'll learn: A+ Core 1 skill map</h2>
  <p>Here's the typical competency map from course completion to exam readiness for 220-1201:</p>

  <h3>By exam domain:</h3>

  <h4>Mobile Devices (13%)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Install and configure laptop hardware and components (screen, keyboard, battery, RAM)</li>
    <li>Configure mobile device network connectivity (Wi-Fi, cellular, Bluetooth, NFC)</li>
    <li>Troubleshoot common mobile device issues (boot loops, touchscreen unresponsive, battery drain)</li>
    <li>Understand mobile operating systems (iOS, Android, Windows 10/11 mobile features)</li>
    <li>Configure security settings (screen lock, Find My Device, encryption)</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Networking (23%)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Explain TCP/IP basics (IPv4 addressing, subnetting basics, default gateway, DNS)</li>
    <li>Install and configure wired/wireless small office/home office (SOHO) networks</li>
    <li>Configure wireless security (WPA2-Personal, WPA3, SSID, MAC filtering)</li>
    <li>Explain common port and protocol numbers (22 SSH, 80 HTTP, 443 HTTPS, 3389 RDP, 25 SMTP)</li>
    <li>Compare network types (LAN, WAN, PAN, MAN) and their typical use cases</li>
    <li>Basic cloud connectivity concepts (VPN, cloud network architecture)</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Hardware (25%)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Identify and compare CPU types (Intel Core, AMD Ryzen, features: hyperthreading, overclocking)</li>
    <li>Install and configure RAM types (DDR3, DDR4, DDR5, SO-DIMM form factors)</li>
    <li>Install and configure storage devices (SATA, NVMe SSD, HDD, external drives)</li>
    <li>Install power supplies and explain wattage, efficiency ratings (80+ Bronze/Gold/Platinum)</li>
    <li>Disassemble and reassemble laptops and all-in-one PCs</li>
    <li>Troubleshoot common hardware failures (no POST, overheating, component incompatibility)</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Virtualization and Cloud Computing (11%)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Explain the difference between type-1 (bare-metal) and type-2 (hosted) hypervisors (VMware ESXi, Microsoft Hyper-V, Oracle VirtualBox, KVM)</li>
    <li>Describe cloud service models: IaaS, PaaS, SaaS with examples</li>
    <li>Explain cloud deployment models: public, private, hybrid</li>
    <li>Basic AWS, Azure, GCP concepts (EC2, S3, basic account structure)</li>
    <li>Compare on-premises vs cloud resource pricing models</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Hardware and Network Troubleshooting (28%)</h4>
